 "notes": "Basic Scalar scenario, Fig.2 (green GEO600 exclusion), rho_local=0.4 GeV/cm3. Paper parameterises photon coupling via L_int = (phi/Lambda_gamma) F^2/4, i.e. delta_alpha/alpha = phi/Lambda_gamma; converted to Damour-Donoghue d_e using delta_alpha/alpha = d_e*kappa*phi => d_e = (1/Lambda_gamma)/kappa, kappa=sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl=2.906e-19 GeV^-1 (M_Pl=1.22e19 GeV). Y-axis of Fig.2 is 1/Lambda_i in GeV^-1; curve is the lower boundary (deepest reach) of the green region extracted from the vector PDF. Mass axis calibrated via f-to-m (m=h f/c^2), verified left frame=1e-20 eV; band spans GEO600 50-5800 Hz. Since the refractive-index (delta_n) contribution is neglected, the electron-coupling limit (Lambda_e -> d_me) is numerically identical (Eq.6 is symmetric in 1/Lambda_gamma+1/Lambda_e); reporting ScalarPhoton as main plane. Best reach d_e~0.16 (Lambda~2e19 GeV; abstract rounds to 3e19). Limits set assuming the other coupling zero.",
